WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:04.200
MyCampusView Academy. Robotics 101, video 9: Reading the IR sensors.

2
00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:10.623
Before the robot can follow a line, we must be sure it

3
00:00:10.673 --> 00:00:12.472
can see the line.

4
00:00:12.522 --> 00:00:19.650
In this video, you will read both sensors and print what they see.

5
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.390
First we give the pins names.

6
00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:27.612
LEFT_IR is pin 2 and RIGHT_IR is pin 3.

7
00:00:27.662 --> 00:00:31.618
ON_LINE says which value means black.

8
00:00:31.668 --> 00:00:34.650
For many sensors it is HIGH.

9
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:40.126
digitalRead reads a pin and gives HIGH or LOW.

10
00:00:40.176 --> 00:00:44.896
Then we print BLACK or WHITE for each sensor.

11
00:00:44.946 --> 00:00:51.150
The short delay slows the printing down so you can read it.

12
00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.464
Upload the sketch and open the Serial Monitor at 9600 baud.

13
00:00:57.514 --> 00:01:01.242
Slide the robot slowly across the line.

14
00:01:01.292 --> 00:01:07.150
You should see the left sensor say BLACK, then the right one.

15
00:01:07.800 --> 00:01:13.567
If black shows as WHITE, your module is the other way round:

16
00:01:13.617 --> 00:01:15.700
change ON_LINE to LOW.

17
00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:19.869
If a sensor never changes, adjust its knob.

18
00:01:19.919 --> 00:01:23.650
If nothing prints, check the baud rate.

19
00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:30.500
Next: Controlling the motors in code.
